LV

Purpose

LV (Low Voltage) is the first electrical technology tier.

The player transitions from steam-powered industry to electrical machinery and begins building a scalable electrical infrastructure.

LV introduces electrical power generation, distribution, and the first generation of electrically powered industrial machines.

The player should begin replacing inefficient steam-dependent processes with electrical production while maintaining and expanding the infrastructure established during the Steam Age.

Resources

LV primarily uses:

Iron
Copper
Tin
Redstone
Steel
Rubber
Bronze
Brass
Other materials required for electrical infrastructure

Higher-tier materials remain restricted until their respective technological stages.

Tools

LV introduces the first electrically assisted tools and equipment.

These tools should improve resource gathering and industrial construction without providing capabilities intended for higher voltage tiers.

Tools should remain secondary to the development of industrial infrastructure.

Processing

LV introduces electrically powered processing.

Production chains should become faster, more efficient, and increasingly multi-stage.

The player should begin producing components specifically for electrical machinery and infrastructure.

LV processing should establish the production chains required for advancing into MV.

Machines

LV introduces the first major electrical machines.

Machines should provide:

Basic electrical processing
Material refining
Component manufacturing
Resource processing
Electrical automation
Early industrial production

LV machines should be significantly more efficient than Steam-tier machinery while remaining limited by LV power generation and throughput.

Higher-tier machines remain locked.

Power

Electricity becomes the primary power system of LV.

The player must establish:

Electrical generation
Power storage where appropriate
Electrical distribution
Reliable power production
Sufficient power capacity for industrial machinery

Steam remains useful as an industrial power source and may be used to support electrical generation.

Power generation should require infrastructure and resource investment rather than functioning as an unlimited source of energy.

Automation

LV allows the player to build the first fully automated electrical production lines.

Automation may include:

Automated ore processing
Automated component production
Machine chains
Item transportation
Power distribution
Resource buffering
Continuous production

The scale of automation should increase substantially compared to the Steam Age.

However, production throughput remains limited by LV machinery and power capacity.

Create Integration

Create remains available as a mechanical and logistical system.

Create should primarily provide:

Mechanical automation
Item transportation
Factory infrastructure
Material handling
Mechanical processing

Create should complement electrical machinery rather than replace it.

Create systems must not provide a cheaper alternative to LV technological progression.

GregTech Integration

GregTech defines the primary technological progression of LV.

GregTech materials, machines, components, and processing chains should establish the requirements for advancing toward MV.

LV should require the player to construct dedicated electrical infrastructure rather than simply upgrading existing Steam machines.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization provides additional electrical machinery and processing capabilities.

Its systems should be integrated into the same LV progression and share the technological requirements established by the pack.

Modern Industrialization must not create an independent progression path that bypasses GregTech's technological gates.

Mekanism Integration

Mekanism becomes available as a supporting industrial system during LV.

Its machines should provide specialized processing and utility capabilities while remaining subject to the same progression restrictions as other industrial systems.

Mekanism must not provide early access to processing or power capabilities intended for higher technological tiers.

Requirements

The player must complete the Steam Age before entering LV.

The player should have:

Established a functioning Steam infrastructure
Automated essential Steam-era production
Produced the components required for electrical machinery
Established the required electrical materials
Built the infrastructure necessary for electrical power generation

Exit Condition

LV ends when the player has established a stable and scalable electrical industry capable of supporting the increased complexity of MV.

The player must:

Establish reliable electrical generation
Automate essential LV production chains
Produce the components required for MV machinery
Expand electrical infrastructure beyond basic LV capacity
Complete the required LV production chains

Completion of these requirements unlocks MV.

The LV stage should leave the player with a functioning electrical factory capable of supporting the next technological tier.
